{
 "id": "2026-abatti-large",
 "name": "Large Wood in Rivers: Photo Questionnaire",
 "description": "Faithful replication with the paper's own stimuli: participants first answer questions about education, area of expertise, occupation and residence, then rate ten photographs of Brazilian river corridors (five with large wood in the channel, five without) on aesthetic, naturalness, hazard and need for improvement with one to three stars. A moderate or high hazard or improvement rating opens a short \"why\" box. Only after the photos are they asked what they think of wood inside river channels. Photos, criteria definitions, background categories and the final question are taken from Abatti et al. (2026), Environmental Management 76: 183 (Fig. 1, Methods, Table 1; CC BY 4.0), and the paper's mean scores are stored for comparison. Differences from the original study: (1) the panel letters were cropped off the top of each photo, and photos are the size printed in the figure (about 390 px wide); (2) photo order is random; the paper does not state its order; (3) \"Other\" options and the beneficial / detrimental / it depends choice before the final \"why\" are our wording; (4) the paper's sample was adults in Brazil reached through academic and professional networks.",
